<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  telemetry:exempt static string resources, not a user-facing surface — a resource file has no
  user action and no error path. The module's telemetry is wired in the @HiltViewModels in :app
  (CountsViewModel / BirthDeathViewModel / ShiftingViewModel): AnalyticsEvents constants via
  AnalyticsPort.track, plus CrashReporter.recordException on every refresh and enqueue failure.

  Counts module chrome strings: the census read screen plus the two write forms
  (birth/death, shifting).

  Scope note (AGENTS.md golden frontend rule): these cover STATIC chrome only —
  screen titles, field labels, group headings, and hint text. Every live value the
  operator actually reads or writes (park/shed identities, breeds, management
  stages, totals, rejection copy) is backend-owned and arrives through the app
  contract, never from this file. The same split feature-sheds uses.
-->
